The original spec was wrong for p = 30. A 30-point winner must have reached 30 from 29 with the loser at 28 or 29, since any lower loser score would have ended the game earlier by the win-by-two rule. The p = 21 and 22 to 29 cases are correct, and the new spec encodes all three.

```python
def pre(p):
    return And(p >= 21, p <= 30)

def post(p, r):
    # Winner has p points (21 <= p <= 30); r is the loser's final score.
    # p == 21: game ended at 21 with a lead of at least 2, so 0 <= r <= 19.
    # 22 <= p <= 29: the winner first gets a lead of 2 at p, so r == p - 2.
    # p == 30: the game was at 29 with the loser at 28 or 29 (not yet ended),
    #          then the winner scored to 30, so r is 28 or 29.
    return And(
        Implies(p == 21, And(r >= 0, r <= 19)),
        Implies(And(p >= 22, p <= 29), r == p - 2),
        Implies(p == 30, And(r >= 28, r <= 29)),
    )
```
